From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:45:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: [Anti Detection] TEE Soft Emu - Keep
 ATTEST_KEY RootOfTrust coherent

Certificate processing was gated only on ATTESTATION_CHALLENGE, while
PURPOSE_ATTEST_KEY creation commonly omits the challenge.

This left such ATTEST_KEY entries with incomplete signer metadata.
Keys later generated through the UserGenerated attestation path kept
their original hardware RootOfTrust, while the RKP path was patched to
the virtual locked and verified state, exposing a deterministic
cross-path divergence.

Process certificate responses for both challenged requests and
ATTEST_KEY creation. When the original self-signed ATTEST_KEY
certificate has no attestation extension and cannot use the normal
patch-and-resign path, select a validated native keybox identity and
persist its matching signer material.

This keeps RKP and explicit ATTEST_KEY paths on the same virtual
RootOfTrust and preserves a verifiable certificate chain across the
ATTEST_KEY lifecycle.

Add a regression test for ATTEST_KEY creation without an attestation
challenge.

Change-Id: Ie8397e40e4fb2e290d723a4a51397a9e81618838
